  "apod": {
    "date": "2026-11-03",
    "title": "Comet PanSTARRs and Rainbow Meteor",
    "explanation": " Explanation:  Did this meteor come from that comet? Probably not. Although many  meteors  do originate from comets, there are  thousands  of  comets  that have visited the inner  Solar System  recently, and matching meteors to them can be tricky. And to be clear, the  pictured comet  is far behind the  streaking meteor . Comet  C/2025 R3 (PanSTARRS)  was captured from  Hautacam ,  France  in April when the  giant space iceberg  sported impressive  ion  (blue) and dust  tails . Sand-sized rocky debris that enters  Earth’s atmosphere  typically appears as  meteors , while the  colorful foreground streak  here may indicate a complicated composition. This month three  notable meteor showers  will reach their peaks. Over the next few days, the Southern  Taurids  will be reaching their apex, while the Northern  Taurids  will top out about a week later. Both originate from  Comet 2P/Encke . November is most famous for the  Leonids Meteor Shower , though, which originates from  Comet 55P/Tempel-Tuttle  and will  reach its crescendo  in about two weeks.   Tomorrow's picture:  open space",
    "image": "https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/CometMeteor_Metais_1934.jpg?w=0&h=0&fit=clip&crop=faces,focalpoint",
    "link": "https://science.nasa.gov/image-article/apod-2026-november-3-comet-panstarrs-and-rainbow-meteor/",
    "credit": " Eddy Metais ",
    "alt": "A comet with a long flowing tail is seen below a star-filled  sky and above a peaked hill. Starting right in the tail of the comet is a multicolored meteor. Please see the explanation for more detailed information.",
    "media_type": "image"
  },
  "updated": "2026-11-03T08:59:30.284589+00:00"
